# MUCL Usage Guidelines

> Sourced from MUCL component Storybook documentation. This is a living document — coverage will expand as new `.mdx` files are approved. What is here is correct; gaps are expected.

Rules are classified as **Hard** (AI must refuse/redirect) or **Soft** (AI should suggest the better alternative).

---

## Component Selection Decision Tree

These rules resolve the most common "which component?" decisions. Apply them before building.

### Interactive vs. non-interactive indicators

| Need | Use | Not |
|---|---|---|
| Static status label, count, or category | `m-badge` | `m-chip` |
| Removable tag, selectable filter, interactive choice | `m-chip` | `m-badge` |

Classification: **Hard**

### Checkbox vs. Radio vs. Switch

| Need | Use | Not |
|---|---|---|
| Multiple selections from a group | `m-checkbox` | `m-radio` |
| Single selection from a group of 2+ | `m-radio` | `m-checkbox` |
| Binary on/off that takes immediate effect | `m-switch` | `m-checkbox` |
| Binary choice that requires form submission | `m-checkbox` | `m-switch` |
| Single option on its own (agreement, opt-in) | `m-checkbox` | `m-radio` |

Classification: **Hard** — Checkboxes = selection, switches = activation. Do not interchange.

### Button vs. ButtonLink

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| In-page action (submit, toggle, open modal) | `m-button` |
| Navigation to a route or URL | `m-button-link` |

Classification: **Hard**

### Menu vs. Select vs. Popup

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Choose one value for a form field | `m-select` |
| Open a list of commands or actions | `m-button-menu` |
| Show arbitrary content (card) anchored to a trigger | `m-button-popup` |

Classification: **Hard**

### Split Button vs. Menu Button

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| One default/primary action + related secondary options | `m-split-button` |
| All options are equal, no default action | `m-button-menu` |

Classification: **Hard**

### Popup vs. Modal

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| User needs to see underlying page while interacting | `m-popup` |
| Alert, confirmation, or focused task | `m-modal` |

Classification: **Soft** — Prefer modals in most cases.

### Skeleton vs. Spinner

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Structure of upcoming content is known | `m-skeleton` |
| Structure is unknown or area is small | `m-spinner` |
| Content-heavy layout (tables, trees, blades) | `m-skeleton` |
| Background or non-critical loading | `m-spinner` |

Classification: **Hard** for structure-known rule; **Soft** for preferences.

### Input vs. Inline Input

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Standalone form field | `m-input` |
| Fill-in-the-blank within a sentence or paragraph | `m-inline-input` |

Classification: **Hard** — Do not use inline input as a general form field replacement.

### Table vs. List

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Structured data with at least 2 rows and consistent columns | `m-datatable` |
| Content without a consistent columnar pattern | Other layout |

Classification: **Hard**

### Accordion: when NOT to use

Do not use `m-accordion` when:
- Content must be read in full (use paragraph text)
- There is too little content to justify collapsing (adds cognitive load)
- The layout already shows clear hierarchy without collapsing

Classification: **Hard**

---

## Per-Component Usage Rules

### m-accordion

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Keep header text to 50–75 characters per line | Soft |
| Cap row width at 1080px to keep title and end icons visually connected | Soft |
| Use color on headers sparingly and only for semantic meaning | Soft |

### m-badge

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Every badge must have a `label` — no icon-only badges | Hard |
| Use sentence case for badge labels | Soft |
| Do not cluster multiple badges on one element; use one badge for the primary status and plain text for extras | Soft |
| Do not place `m-accent` (important/navy) badges near filled action buttons — they look identical | Soft |
| Add a border when badge-to-background contrast is below 3:1 | Soft |

**Variant intent mapping:**

| Variant | Use for |
|---|---|
| `m-accent` / `m-accent-subtle` | Critical callouts requiring attention |
| `m-positive` / `m-positive-subtle` | Success, completion, met criteria |
| `m-negative` / `m-negative-subtle` | Errors, denials, failures |
| `m-warning` / `m-warning-subtle` | Caution, risks, pre-submission checks |
| `m-info` / `m-info-subtle` | Tips, supplementary context |
| `m-highlight` / `m-highlight-subtle` | New features, special items, unmet quantifiers |

Use standard variants for primary-focus status; subtle variants when status is secondary or UI is visually dense.

### m-button

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Maximum one primary (`m-filled` or `m-negative`) button per page | Hard |
| Every button must have a label (use `hideLabel` for icon-only, not omission) | Hard |
| Use verbs for button labels ("Save", "Cancel"), not nouns or adjectives | Soft |
| Use sentence case for button labels | Soft |
| Icons go in leading position only; no trailing icons (except dropdown carets) | Hard |
| Do not use icons as decoration — only when they clarify the action | Soft |
| Do not override button styles or use custom colors | Hard |
| Place primary button to the right of secondary buttons | Soft |

**Button hierarchy:**

| Variant | Role |
|---|---|
| `m-filled` | Primary action (one per page) |
| `m-negative` | Destructive/irreversible action (one per page, instead of m-filled) |
| `m-outline` | Secondary actions |
| `m-inverted` | Secondary on dark backgrounds |
| `m-text` | Tertiary actions (use sparingly) |

### m-card

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Do not nest cards inside other cards | Hard |
| Keep card content focused — title, body, relevant actions | Soft |
| Use `m-bordered` for display-only cards, `m-tonal` for subdued content, `m-interactive` when the entire card is clickable | Soft |

### m-checkbox

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Every checkbox group must have a descriptive group label | Hard |
| Use indeterminate state when a parent checkbox represents mixed child values | Hard |
| Use disabled (not hidden) for controls that will activate later in the workflow | Soft |

### m-chip

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Keep chip labels under 20 characters | Soft |
| Use sentence case for chip labels | Soft |
| Leading icon = primary action or category; trailing icon = secondary action (dismiss, expand) | Soft |

### m-datatable

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| No zebra stripes (alternating row colors) — row dividers are sufficient | Hard |
| Left-align text; right-align numbers (except nominal numbers: ZIP, phone, ordinals) | Hard |
| Column headers must match the alignment of their data | Hard |
| Center-align only for badges, icons, or very small content — never for regular text or numbers | Hard |
| Use en dash (–) for missing or N/A cell values | Soft |
| Aim for 5–7 columns maximum to avoid horizontal scrolling | Soft |
| Use pagination for large datasets (10–15 rows per page) | Soft |

### m-date-picker

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| A label is required (can be visually hidden) | Hard |

### m-icon

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Use icons to support text, not replace it — if meaning is unclear, use a text label instead | Hard |
| Solid style = active/selected state; regular (outline) style = inactive/unselected state | Soft |

### m-inline-input

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Use only for fill-in-the-blank within running text — never as standalone form fields | Hard |
| A label is required (usually visually hidden) | Hard |
| No room for help text — use `m-tooltip` for guidance if needed | Soft |

### m-input

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| A label is required — unlabeled fields are not acceptable | Hard |
| Use sentence case for labels and placeholder text | Hard |
| Do not use placeholder text for instructions — use help text instead | Hard |
| Do not duplicate the same text in both placeholder and help text | Hard |
| Error text should be user-focused, offer a solution, and end with a period | Soft |

### m-menu / m-menu-item

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Every menu item must have a `label` | Hard |

### m-popup

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Must have a `title` attribute | Hard |
| Avoid showing multiple popups at once | Soft |

### m-radio / m-radio-group

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Radio buttons must be used in groups — never standalone | Hard |
| Group must have a `groupLabel` (can be visually hidden) | Hard |
| All options in a group must be mutually exclusive | Hard |
| Prefer `m-radio-group` with an `options` array over individual `m-radio` elements | Soft |
| Use sentence case for labels | Soft |

### m-select

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| A label is required — placeholder is not a substitute | Hard |
| Use sentence case for labels and placeholder text | Soft |
| Size the field width to show the full selected value without truncation | Soft |

### m-skeleton

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Skeleton layout must approximate the final content (size, shape, alignment) | Soft |
| Use neutral, muted placeholder colors | Hard |
| Avoid overuse — skip skeletons for content that loads quickly (causes flicker) | Soft |

### m-spinner

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Use indeterminate when duration is unknown; determinate when progress is quantifiable | Soft |
| Show only one spinner at a time | Soft |
| Size by context: xl = full-page, l = large area, m = panel/modal, s = inline/button | Soft |
| Label should be specific ("Preparing results…") not generic ("Loading…") | Soft |

### m-split-button

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Must have a `label` | Hard |

### m-switch

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| A label is required (can be hidden via `labelPosition`) | Hard |
| Use a noun or short noun phrase for the label (describes the setting) | Soft |
| Switches do not support error state — use checkbox if validation is needed | Soft |

### m-tooltip

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Never use tooltips as the only way to convey critical information | Hard |
| Never place interactive elements (buttons, links) inside tooltips | Hard |
| Do not restate information already visible on the page | Hard |
| Keep content to one or two short sentences | Soft |
| Limit icon usage to `circle-info`, `triangle-exclamation`, or `circle-check` | Soft |

---

## Cross-Cutting Rules

These apply to all components:

| Rule | Type |
|---|---|
| Use sentence case for all user-facing labels and text | Soft |
| Every input-like component (input, select, date picker, radio group, inline input) must have a label | Hard |
| Icons support text — they do not replace it | Hard |
| Variant selection should follow semantic intent, not color preference | Hard |
| Standard variants for primary emphasis; subtle variants for secondary or dense layouts | Soft |
